{
  "spec_version": 1,
  "description": "Shared golden test vectors for every lightkeeper implementation (Python, ESP32 firmware, and Swift). All three test suites must pass every case, which keeps the implementations in lockstep. A case gives either one raw Nightscout `entry` (or null) with its age as `minutes_ago` or `seconds_ago`, or an `entries` list whose items each hold an `entry` and its own age; every entry is parsed, bad ones are skipped, and the newest survivor (the lower value on a timestamp tie) is classified. `error` is an optional fetch error. `thresholds` optionally replaces the defaults with `urgent_low`, `low`, `high`, `urgent_high` (mg/dL) and `stale_after_minutes`, all five given and valid. Default thresholds: 55 / 70 / 180 / 250 mg/dL, stale after 15 minutes. `level` and `lines` are the exact expected result. spec_version increments whenever an existing case changes; adding a case or an optional field does not bump it.",
